{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2","c3","c4"],"primary":"c3","title":"Prohibition of Anti-Competitive Automated Rent Price-Fixing Ordinance","requirement":"It is unlawful to sell, license, or otherwise provide an algorithmic device to a landlord, and unlawful for a landlord to use one to set rental rates or occupancy levels for residential rental property. An algorithmic device is software or a product that runs algorithms on nonpublic competitor data to recommend rents or occupancy levels; tenants may sue for injunctive relief, damages, or civil penalties, plus costs and attorney's fees.","key_value":"Civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation; each month of use and each affected property is a separate violation","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"San Diego Mun. Code §§ 98.1101–98.1104","coverage_conditions":"All residential rental property in the City of San Diego; applies to landlords and to persons who sell, license, or provide algorithmic devices.","exemptions":"(a) Software or products that publish reports on rental rates or occupancy levels using aggregated historical nonpublic competitor data more than 90 days old, or publicly available information, and that do not recommend rates or occupancy levels for future leases or renewals; (b) software or products used to set rental rates or income limits under local, state, or federal affordable housing program guidelines.","coverage_from":"c3","conflict_note":"Status and effective date disagree. The official document D076 (c3) is the proposed ordinance text and shows no adoption, so it reports status pending with no effective date. Secondary sources D002 (c1) and D037 (c2) report the ordinance in force effective 2025-06, and D086 (c4) states San Diego has already banned the software. Status is kept as in_force on the weight of the later secondary reports. Effective date is left null because the sources give only a month (2025-06), not a full date, and the official text does not confirm adoption."}],"dropped":[]}
